WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
I want to bring in Max Boot now.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:01.768
He's a senior

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.535
fellow at the Council

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.370
on Foreign Relations.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.437
He has a new column

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.605
in The Washington Post,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.340
and he writes that while it's great,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.875
The Grinder is back home,

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.678
the hostage bazaar has to close.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:12.512
John Avlon, Margaret

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.014
Hoover are back with us also.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:14.581
So, Max,

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.116
when you say the hostage bazaar

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.851
has to end, meaning prisoner swaps.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.118
Yeah.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.818
I mean, there's just been

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.320
so many in recent years.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.454
And it's kind of ironic

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.489
to see

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.356
former President

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.357
Trump and his supporters

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.558
attacking this deal

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.060
when Donald Trump himself bragged

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.194
that he was the greatest

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.963
hostage negotiator in human history.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.663
He made a lot of press.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.965
He made a lot of prisoner swaps

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.267
with the Taliban or the Houthis

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.169
with a lot of repugnant regimes.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.937
And this has been a trend going back

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:38.838
many years now.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.006
And you know, the problem

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.674
is that each individual case,

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.942
our hearts go out to that.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.477
We want to see these Americans come home

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.946
because they are being unjustly detained.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.248
The problem is

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.883
when we are making all these deals,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.984
making all these concessions,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.951
including letting somebody

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.286
like Victor Boot,

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.321
this notorious arms dealer

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.257
out of prison to get somebody else

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.025
who was unjustly detained home

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.560
it creates incentives

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.228
to seize more American hostages.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:02.695
Understand.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.630
But what's the option?

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.364
Let Brittney Griner

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.032
stay in a Russian penal colony.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.533
No, I mean, I'm

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.201
very glad that Brittney Griner is up,

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.302
but I think we need to have a

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.136
serious debate

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:10.804
about whether we want

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.704
to continue doing this

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.173
or whether we should say,

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:13.473
you know,

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:13.873
the State

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.675
Department has a list of countries

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.111
where advises Americans not to travel,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.113
including Russia, Iran, Syria,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.881
some of the obvious candidates.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.016
And maybe at some point

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:23.950
we need to have a president

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.684
who says,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.118
okay, I'm

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.519
going to work to get the people out

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.188
who are currently in prison.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.322
But in the future,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.124
if you choose to go to Russia,

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.058
you are on your own.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.560
We are not going to make concessions

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.260
to get you home.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.794
And by the way,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.495
I might add there

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:38.665
still like 30 American basketball players

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.234
who are still playing in Russia

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.435
as we speak.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.070
That is not very wise.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.538
That is creating the potential

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.606
for yet another hostage

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.408
crisis down the road.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.676
What I think is fascinating about it

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.610
is the idea of

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.012
and some people will ask the question,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.913
but they'll say, well,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:54.747
and I remember

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.015
when she was first detained,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.584
we first learned about her detention

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.218
before people realize

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.420
she was a basketball player there.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.221
They would make comments

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.455
about what someone do in there

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:02.989
because we remember

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.791
we learned about her during the invasion.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.092
She'd already been detained

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.794
or questions about this person

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.129
not a traveler's place on the

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.164
do not do not travel area.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:11.931
But your point really

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.800
is the idea of a hold on

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.103
if people are intending to do it anyway.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:17.904
They ought

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.738
not to be able

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.806
to have the luxury

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.875
of having the government

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.743
support them and have their safe

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.011
return guaranteed.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.212
What do you guys think about that?

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.749
I, I respectfully disagree.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:30.150
I understand

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.951
the point that Max is making,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.053
but I think that the privileges

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:34.888
and responsibilities

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.422
of American citizenship of government

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.490
to its citizens

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.258
don't stop

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:38.625
simply

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.160
because someone has found themselves

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.529
in an unwise or dangerous place.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.864
I haven't yet seen the point

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.698
the max is making,

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.533
which is that, you know,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.867
if you negotiate for

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.835
for one hostage,

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:49.836
that it creates an incentive

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.271
to get another dozen.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.739
Now, on the surface, obviously,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.806
trading someone whose nickname

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.874
is The Merchant of Death

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.142
for a WNBA star

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.377
who was improperly

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.812
detained is an imbalance.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.247
But American presidents

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:01.681
going back

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.949
decades, as Max points out,

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:03.750
have made it a priority

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.951
to try to get Americans

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.652
out of harm's way.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.186
That's a basic

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.587
responsibility of the government

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.955
and the president.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.256
And the fact that she was being used

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:10.757
as a pawn

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.692
within the context of the run up

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.460
to the invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.895
Paul Whalen still is there.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.130
He should be released.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.131
But I think we need to celebrate

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:18.631
as Americans.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.332
What we need to avoid

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.800
is the kind of situational ethics

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.335
we see where Republicans

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.970
who celebrated every hostage

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.572
released by Donald Trump condemn

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.040
this one is making America weaker.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.474
It does not make us weaker.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:28.841
Well, no,

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:29.943
I mean I mean, I agree with you.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.277
There is massive hypocrisy

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.812
on the part of Republicans here.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.913
There's no way around that.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.548
But I think at the end of the day,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.317
there is a legitimate point that these

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.618
that these hostage swaps

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.485
do make us weaker.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.254
The problem is both parties have done it.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.122
It's a bipartisan problem.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:43.990
Margaret, what do you think?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.524
What do you do?

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:48.094
I mean, I am willing to give a lot of

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.331
leeway to the people

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.498
who are in the negotiations

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.733
and who have the intelligence,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.034
who know the details about

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.502
what was being offered

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.771
between Brittany and Paul Whalen.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.273
I'm delighted that she's home.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.609
Of course, we've been following it.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.778
But if I recall, President Trump slapped

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.716
many, many dozens of Taliban prisoners,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:10.583
which

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.452
which struck me as an outrage at the time

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.753
in order to get Americans back.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.520
But you're right,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.421
there is this precedent

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.090
for four American presidents

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:17.890
doing what they can

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.892
in order to get Americans back.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.463
I was struck, frankly, that her statement

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:23.830
that she

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.964
she took time in her statement

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.799
to update the country about how she was,

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.335
but then to also make note of Poland,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.337
who is still there in Russia.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.306
And there has been a degree of criticism

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.308
about him being left behind

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.676
and some commentary about that.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.445
I, I wasn't part of the negotiations.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.780
I mean, basically, why don't you.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.015
But what does that mean?

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.182
There's a lot of opportunism

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:43.750
there, obviously.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.551
Because, I mean, everybody wants Paul

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:45.985
Whalen home.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.421
But he was captured in 20, 18

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.789
when Donald Trump was president.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.923
And now Trump

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.325
and others are suggesting that Biden

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.092
did something wrong by

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:53.726
not getting him out.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:54.427
Well, why didn't Trump

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.695
get him out in the first place?

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.362
Yeah, great point.

